course: dictionary
lesson: 10089
title: The thermometer
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A thermometer is an instrument, which means a tool, that measures temperature. Temperature tells us how hot or cold something is. «Vets often take a pet's temperature with a thermometer under the tail, because it gives an accurate reading.» Accurate means correct, close to the true answer.
explain: Use the clues around the word. «How cold it is can be checked with a window, a thermometer or a weather app; one person's feeling is not the measurement.» The sentence says a thermometer gives a measurement, which is a number, not a guess.
explain: Thermometers use degrees. In science we read them in degrees Celsius (°C), and in the USA people often use Fahrenheit (°F). Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: "a tool that measures how hot or cold something is" fits, so you understand the word.
fact: A thermometer is an instrument that measures temperature.
fact: Temperature tells us how hot or cold something is.
fact: A medical thermometer measures body temperature to check for a fever.
fact: Normal body temperature is about 37 °C (98.6 °F); 38 °C or more is a fever.
fact: Old glass thermometers may contain mercury, which is poisonous, so a grown-up must clean up a broken one.
exercise: «Vets often take a pet's temperature with a thermometer under the tail.» What does a thermometer measure? | The colour of its fur | *How hot or cold something is | The sound a pet makes | The weight of a pet
exercise: «Old glass thermometers may contain mercury, which is poisonous, so a grown-up must clean up a broken one.» Why must a grown-up clean up a broken one? | *Because mercury is poisonous | Because glass is too heavy to lift | Because grown-ups like tidying | Because the thermometer is always too hot to touch
exercise: A child has a medical thermometer reading of 39 °C. Is this a fever? | No, 39 °C is normal body temperature | 37 °C is a fever | 36 °C is a fever | *Yes, 38 °C or more is a fever
test: «How cold it is can be checked with a window, a thermometer or a weather app; one person's feeling is not the measurement.» What does the sentence say is better than one person's feeling? | *A measurement from a thermometer | Wearing a warm coat | Looking out of the window and feeling cold | A friend's guess
test: What is a thermometer? | A kind of weather map | *An instrument that measures temperature | A tool that measures length | A type of soft drink
exam: In science lessons, which unit do we read a thermometer in? | Litres | Metres | *Degrees Celsius (°C) | Kilograms
